<p>The three day bilateral gap between the average RMG's of the UK and Austria on Tuesday exceeded six percent at 6.244. The 3-day (six percent) rule has therefore been triggered and sterling will enter the first of up to five 10-day confirmation periods on Wednesday, prior to a possible revaluation on June 5, 1997. All green rate devaluations are supended until the successful completion of the first confirmation period when all currencies with negative RMG's will be devalued by reducing their gaps to zero. The first confirmation period will run from April 16-25. During confirmation periods the 3-day (6 percent) rule is suspended.</p>
